<title>SOUTH KOREA: Shares in S.Korean shipbuilders up on brisk orders.</title>
<headline>Shares in S.Korean shipbuilders up on brisk orders.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Daewoo Heavy Industries Co and two other South Korean shipbuilding firms rose on Friday morning on news that foreign ship orders had soared in the first half of the year, brokers said.</p>
<p>The three firms briefly rose to their daily limits before retreating on profit-taking. Daewoo was up 360 won to 8,460, Hanjin Heavy Industries Co up 280 won to 9,400 and Samsung Heavy Industries Co up 700 won to 11,300.</p>
</text>
